WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.400 --> 00:00:10.340
In 1977, a severe drought struck Daphne Major, a small island in the Galápagos.

2
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:13.860
Most of its medium ground finches died.

3
00:00:14.840 --> 00:00:17.740
The birds left had deeper beaks, on average.

4
00:00:18.940 --> 00:00:21.000
Researchers had measured them before the drought.

5
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.920
So did the drought change the birds, or change which were left?

6
00:00:26.833 --> 00:00:30.353
Natural selection needs three things at once.

7
00:00:31.093 --> 00:00:36.233
First, variation. Variation means the differences among individuals.

8
00:00:37.433 --> 00:00:38.733
Second, inheritance.

9
00:00:39.533 --> 00:00:43.393
An inherited trait is carried in genes from parent to young.

10
00:00:44.313 --> 00:00:46.253
Third, unequal success.

11
00:00:47.013 --> 00:00:50.693
The differences change how many offspring an individual leaves.

12
00:00:51.733 --> 00:00:54.073
A mutation is a change in DNA.

13
00:00:54.593 --> 00:00:57.093
It is the source of new versions of genes.

14
00:00:58.113 --> 00:01:00.113
Selection does not make variation.

15
00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.413
It sorts what is already there.

16
00:01:03.233 --> 00:01:08.753
Fitness is how many offspring an individual leaves that survive to reproduce.

17
00:01:09.793 --> 00:01:15.573
An adaptation is an inherited trait that helps an organism survive and reproduce in

18
00:01:15.573 --> 00:01:16.713
its present environment.

19
00:01:17.993 --> 00:01:21.193
On Daphne Major, a deep beak was an adaptation.

20
00:01:22.253 --> 00:01:26.113
Large birds, especially males with large beaks, survived best.

21
00:01:26.853 --> 00:01:30.433
They could crack the large, hard seeds left after the drought.

22
00:01:31.267 --> 00:01:34.547
No bird's beak grew because of the drought.

23
00:01:35.327 --> 00:01:39.887
The birds that died were, on average, different from the birds that lived.

24
00:01:41.107 --> 00:01:47.027
Beak size is strongly inherited, so the next generation's beaks were deeper too, on

25
00:01:47.027 --> 00:01:52.927
average. The inherited change tends to last, unless the environment later favours

26
00:01:52.927 --> 00:01:53.927
something else.

27
00:01:54.550 --> 00:01:57.050
How can one species become two?

28
00:01:57.950 --> 00:02:03.030
A species is a group of organisms that can interbreed and produce fertile offspring.

29
00:02:04.090 --> 00:02:08.990
Speciation is when one species splits into groups that can no longer do that.

30
00:02:09.690 --> 00:02:12.230
It often starts with geographic isolation.

31
00:02:12.870 --> 00:02:16.190
That is a barrier, such as a river, between the groups.

32
00:02:16.950 --> 00:02:21.310
On each side, different mutations arise and different traits are favoured.

33
00:02:22.230 --> 00:02:25.050
Separation alone is not speciation, though.

34
00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:27.150
Back to the question.

35
00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:31.130
The drought did not reshape any finch's beak.

36
00:02:31.690 --> 00:02:34.470
It changed which birds lived to breed.

37
00:02:35.270 --> 00:02:37.530
Their young inherited deeper beaks.

38
00:02:38.410 --> 00:02:44.070
One species can become two when separated groups change in different ways until they

39
00:02:44.070 --> 00:02:45.670
can no longer interbreed.

40
00:02:46.470 --> 00:02:49.630
Selection sorts the differences that already exist.
